=== 6. Repeated copies keep the lifecycle chain bounded (gh-ocannl-1623) ===
a compiled destination has a lifecycle ancestor: true
copies into an existing buffer: every sampled ledger size is the initial one: true
copies into an existing buffer: every sampled depth is the initial one: true
copies into an existing buffer: each changed value reached the destination: true
a fresh root is at depth 0: true
a fresh destination, then overwrites: every sampled ledger size is the initial one: true
a fresh destination, then overwrites: every sampled depth is 0: true
a fresh destination, then overwrites: each changed value reached it: true
merge-buffer fills: every sampled ledger size is the initial one: true
merge-buffer fills: every sampled depth is the initial one: true
the consumer compiled after the fills reads the last one: true
a consumer of a superseded fill is refused, naming the fill: true
releasing a copy's result releases its destination: true
releasing the destination again is harmless: true
releasing the destination releases a copy's result: true
